Error [jet.MissingDisplay]: `ParseError` has no `Display` implementation
  --> tests/ui/E0915_names_a_type_without_display_once.jet:5:31
    |
  5 |         print("couldn't read {err}")
    |                               ^^^
 Why: Bare `{value}` interpolation calls `Display` — there is no default for user types
 Fix: Add `impl ParseError.Display { display: fn(self) -> String { … } }`, or use `{value:Debug}` for debug output
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0915
